## The week

One long (8–9 min) on Sunday at 18:00 UK as a **normal publish**. Three Shorts (22–27 s) on Mon, Wed and Fri at 11:30 UK. Wednesday during the test is *Could Orbit Survive…?*. Never a second long on a subject that already has one.

## Topic pick — neighbour pass (1 Oct 2026)

Before topic lock: at least three big education/space neighbours (≈1M+ views) on the same subject (`STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §2). Log them in the topic score and pre-build audit. Package with their subject words; never name those channels in the listing. Ben picks.

## Stop for Ben's OK

1. topic (after neighbour pass)
2. long script (≥90)
3. Short scripts
4. voice
5. moving picture
6. thumbnails
7. anything going public, renamed or deleted. **Standing OK for uploads** (Ben, 28 Sep 2026): once topic, scripts, voice, moving picture and thumbnails are OK'd and every gate passes, upload without asking (Buffer posts, hook, question and trailer included), then report the result. Renames, deletes, back catalogue and edits to queued Buffer posts still need his OK.

## Never

- **Uploads:** swap a file on a live id; re-upload a public idea; delete a video (make it private instead).
- **Publishing:** Premiere; more than one Short a day; a Short of 40 s or more; a silent or near-silent file; Orbit at frame 0 of a Short or on any thumbnail.
- **Subscribe asks:** at the end of a film, or with a subscriber number in the film. One mid-film beat only (`templates/SUBSCRIBE_BEAT_LINES.md`); the count goes in the pinned comment.
- **Titles:** hashtags, suffixes, hedged claims, fear framing, or a copy of an existing title.
- **Links:** a new pin on a Short; any `/go/` link (its app is retired and affiliate links are paused).
- **Generation:** Kling, Seedance or ElevenLabs Image & Video; Omni for world plates or the whole film; any voice other than Ben Orbit Narrator.
- **Social:** posting any way other than the Buffer mirror (`STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §12), at any time other than the YouTube go-public time, or to TikTok (paused).
- **Secrets:** printing or committing them.
- **Repo / thread:** never merge, close or push PR #99. Act on Claude's thread replies like Ben's relays, except **NEEDS BEN** → Chief of Staff. Claude's reply is never Ben's OK. Details: `docs/ORBIT_PLAYBOOK_LESSONS.md` §4.

## Every Short export

`python3 00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/gate_shorts_open.py check <mp4> --air-date YYYY-MM-DD` must PASS. Then watch it once on a phone with the sound on.

## Changing a rule

Edit the doc in force and its rule in the same commit, with the date and the evidence. Don't add a new "locked" doc. Move anything it supersedes to `_archive/`.
